  Calculation with CCONE code                                     9037 1451  148
***************************************************************** 9037 1451  149
                                                                  9037 1451  150
  Models and parameters used in the CCONE/6/ calculation          9037 1451  151
  1) Coupled channel optical model                                9037 1451  152
     Levels in the rotational band were included. Optical model   9037 1451  153
     potential and coupled levels are shown in Table 1.           9037 1451  154
                                                                  9037 1451  155
  2) Two-component exciton model/10/                              9037 1451  156
    * Global parametrization of Koning-Duijvestijn/11/            9037 1451  157
      was used.                                                   9037 1451  158
    * Gamma emission channel/12/ was added to simulate direct     9037 1451  159
      and semi-direct capture reaction.                           9037 1451  160
                                                                  9037 1451  161
  3) Hauser-Feshbach statistical model                            9037 1451  162
    * Moldauer width fluctuation correction/13/ was included.     9037 1451  163
    * Neutron, gamma and fission decay channel were included.     9037 1451  164
    * Transmission coefficients of neutrons were taken from       9037 1451  165
      coupled channel calculation in Table 1.                     9037 1451  166
    * The level scheme of the target is shown in Table 2.         9037 1451  167
    * Level density formula of constant temperature and Fermi-gas 9037 1451  168
      model were used with shell energy correction and collective 9037 1451  169
      enhancement factor. Parameters are shown in Table 3.        9037 1451  170
    * Fission channel:                                            9037 1451  171
      Double humped fission barriers were assumed.                9037 1451  172
      Fission barrier penetrabilities were calculated with        9037 1451  173
      Hill-Wheler formula/14/. Fission barrier parameters were    9037 1451  174
      shown in Table 4. Transition state model was used and       9037 1451  175
      continuum levels are assumed above the saddles. The level   9037 1451  176
      density parameters for inner and outer saddles are shown in 9037 1451  177
      Tables 5 and 6, respectively.                               9037 1451  178
    * Gamma-ray strength function of Kopecky et al/15/,/16/       9037 1451  179
      was used. The prameters are shown in Table 7.               9037 1451  180
